Department because of severe chest pain
Starting 20 minutes ago. His past medical
history includes type II diabetes mellitus and
hypertension. On examination, he has a blood
pressure of 110/65 mmHg and pulse of 110
bpm. An ECG shows ST elevation in leads lI,
aVL, V5 and V6. With the diagnosis of ST
elevation myocardial infarction, he undergoes
thrombolytic therapy with tenecteplase followed
by heparin infusion. ST segment elevation
resolves within 20 minutes as does the chest
pain. While heparin is being infused, he
suddenly develops drowsiness and confusion.
His blood pressure is now 185/110 mmHg and
pulse rate 50 bpm. There is no focal
neurological finding. Which one of the following
