department complaining of epigastric pain that
radiates to his lower back. While waiting for
further evaluation in the emergency department,
he suddenly collapses. Physical examination
shows a blood pressure of 80/50 mmHg and
pulse of 110 bpm. He is pale, cold, and sweaty.
