Department by ambulance after he sustained a
gunshot wound to his abdomen. On
examination, he has normal blood pressure and
pulse rate with no sign of hemodynamic
instability. The entry wound is in the
epigastrium. There is no exit wound. The
abdomen is tender to palpation. On anterior-
posterior and lateral abdominal X-ray films, the
bullet is found to be lodged in the right psoas
muscle. Which one of the following would be the
most appropriate next step in management?','{"A":"Emergency ultrasound scan.","B":"Abdominal CT scan.","C":"Close clinical observation.","D":"Exploratory laparotomy.","E":"Diagnostic peritoneal lavage (DPL)."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","supporting_pages":[45],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-2369d62af9e2","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6928decf68aa33b256e5","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","source_page":45,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"6928decf68aa33b256e5","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":45,"supporting_pages":[45],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Emergency Medicine","stem":"A 19-year-old man is brought to the Emergency\nDepartment by ambulance after he sustained a\ngunshot wound to his abdomen. On\nexamination, he has normal blood pressure and\npulse rate with no sign of hemodynamic\ninstability. The entry wound is in the\nepigastrium. There is no exit wound. The\nabdomen is tender to palpation. On anterior-\nposterior and lateral abdominal X-ray films, the\nbullet is found to be lodged in the right psoas\nmuscle. Which one of the following would be the\nmost appropriate next step in management?","options":{"A":"Emergency ultrasound scan.","B":"Abdominal CT scan.","C":"Close clinical observation.","D":"Exploratory laparotomy.","E":"Diagnostic peritoneal lavage (DPL)."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answ