year-old painter, falls off from a height of
approximately three meters and lands on his
both heels before he fell onto the ground. His
coworkers called an ambulance to transfer him
to hospital. In the emergency department, he
denies any loss of consciousness, which is
confirmed by one of his coworkers present at
the scene who has accompanied him to the
hospital. He is fully alert and responsive but in
severe left foot pain and modest right foot
discomfort as well as back pain. There are
abrasions on the palms and a minor wound on
the forehead. Vital signs are all within normal
limits. There is severe tenderness, bruising and
swelling below the left ankle and moderate
tenderness over the lumbar area. Neurological
examination is performed as far as feasible
with unremarkable results. After giving him pain
killers for pain, which one of the following would
be the most appropriate next step in
management?','{"A":"CT scan of the head to exclude\nintracranial hemorrhage.","B":"AP and lateral x-ray films of the left\nand right foot.","C":"scan of the left foot.","D":"Spinal x-ray series.","E":"Immediate referral to orthopedic\nSurgeon."}','D',NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","supporting_pages":[59,60],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-67d854429732","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"8339638125e3a4bf8585","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","source_page":59,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_cross_page_option_stitch","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"8339638125e3a4bf8585","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Emergency Medicine 1.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":59,"supporting_pages":[59,60],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Emergency Medicine","stem":"While doing painting on a scaffold, John, a 48-\nyear-old painter, falls off from a height of\napproximately three meters and lands on his\nboth heels before he fell onto the ground. His\ncoworkers called an ambulance to transfer him\nto hospital. In the emergency department, he\ndenies any loss of consciousness, which is\nconfirmed by one of his coworkers present at\nthe scene who has accompanied him to the\nhospital. He is fully alert and responsive but in\nsevere left foot pain and modest right foot\ndiscomfort as well as back pain. There are\nabrasions on the palms and a minor wound on\nthe forehead. Vital signs are all within normal\nlimits. There is severe tenderness, bruising and\nswelling below the left ankle and moderate\ntenderness over the lumbar a