department after a motor vehicle accident. He
reports hitting his head on the steering wheel
but does not recall the event. He is alert and
oriented on examination, with a Glasgow Coma
scale (GCS) score of 15. He denies any neck
pain and has no focal neurological deficits.
There is no tenderness upon palpation of the
cervical spine. However, he has a severe open
femur fracture with the bone protruding through
the skin and actively bleeding. Based on this
patient''s examination findings, which of the
following statements is true regarding the need
