department after he sustained a bite from a
drunk woman in a pub. The woman was a
stranger who walked away after the incident. On
history, he is fully immunized against tetanus
with the last dose being 3 years ago. He is
unaware of his hepatitis B immunization. On
physical examination, a 2-cm bite wound 5 mm
deep in the right arm is actively bleeding and
teeth marks around the wound. Which of the
following is the most appropriate next step in
