Emergency Department after he sustained a
motor vehicle accident. He is unable to move
his arms and legs, and seems to have cervical
Spine injury. On examination, he has a blood
pressure of 90/60 mmHg and pulse rate of
50bpm. He is alert and is breathing
spontaneously. There is no visible bleeding
source or limb deformity. His chest has
multiple bruises and is tender to touch over
the bruises but is normal on auscultation. The
abdomen is quite normal on exam with no
tenderness, rebound, or guarding. Which one
of the following would be the next best step
