Department with a laceration in his left lower leg
caused by pickax while farming. The wound is
1.5 cm deep and is contaminated with soil. You
debride the wound, disinfect it, and put a non-
adherent bandage on it. On enquiry about
tetanus vaccination, you realize that he had his
tetanus vaccination completed. He also had a
hand cut 5 weeks ago, for which he received a
single dose of dT. Which one of the following is
the appropriate action for management of this
